From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:14:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: let go of what the last draw bound when the target
 changes.

Each draw swaps in a Direct3D device context state of Direct2D's own and
binds the target's render target view and the brushes' views in it, and
nothing ever unbound them: the state held the last target until the next
draw.  A swap chain resized after its back buffer was a target, which is
what a window target of Windows.UI.Composition and a hwnd render target do
when their window changes size, found "something still holding back buffer
0", and the old buffer lived on.

When the target changes, the state is now cleared.  Every draw binds all it
needs again.  Word logged the error 27 times while it started, and no more.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 659973732de5a6e56216e5155e5a0f0f96f23041)

diff --git a/dlls/d2d1/device.c b/dlls/d2d1/device.c
index e10cdd65314..f9febb12cc2 100644
--- a/dlls/d2d1/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/device.c
@@ -2681,11 +2681,36 @@ static void STDMETHODCALLTYPE d2d_device_context_GetDevice(ID2D1DeviceContext6 *
     ID2D1Device_AddRef(*device);
 }
 
+/* Lets go of what the last draw left bound in the Direct3D state of our own: the target's render target view
+ * above all, which kept a swap chain's back buffer from going when it was resized.  Every draw binds all it
+ * needs again. */
+static void d2d_device_context_unbind(struct d2d_device_context *context)
+{
+    ID3DDeviceContextState *prev_state;
+    ID3D11DeviceContext1 *d3d_context;
+
+    if (!context->d3d_state)
+        return;
+
+    if (context->cs)
+        EnterCriticalSection(context->cs);
+    ID3D11Device1_GetImmediateContext1(context->d3d_device, &d3d_context);
+    ID3D11DeviceContext1_SwapDeviceContextState(d3d_context, context->d3d_state, &prev_state);
+    ID3D11DeviceContext1_ClearState(d3d_context);
+    ID3D11DeviceContext1_SwapDeviceContextState(d3d_context, prev_state, NULL);
+    ID3DDeviceContextState_Release(prev_state);
+    ID3D11DeviceContext1_Release(d3d_context);
+    if (context->cs)
+        LeaveCriticalSection(context->cs);
+}
+
 static void d2d_device_context_reset_target(struct d2d_device_context *context)
 {
     if (!context->target.object)
         return;
 
+    d2d_device_context_unbind(context);
+
     if (context->target.type == D2D_TARGET_COMMAND_LIST && context->target.command_list->context == context)
         context->target.command_list->context = NULL;
     IUnknown_Release(context->target.object);
